<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Central Bank director Moura also to leave.</title>
<headline>Brazil Central Bank director Moura also to leave.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Director of Controls at Brazil's Central Bank, Alkimar Moura, is to resign as soon as a successor has been chosen, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Central Bank spokesman said Moura's resignation had been decided a long time ago and was not related to the announcement Tuesday that Central Bank President Gustavo Loyola would step down.</p>
<p>Moura has presided over attempts in the past six months to increase the monetary authority's power of supervision over the banking sector.</p>
</text>
